index e2d80d8c9..a02b21754 100644
--- a/Servex/doc/follow.md
+++ b/Servex/doc/follow.md
@@ -175,6 +175,10 @@ event never fires (the trap above) still delivers every line.
 
 A subscription made by `Agents.follow_child` (it has `of:`) is filtered: `Follow.worth_waking` forwards only the lines `Follow.kind` calls `state` (a task added, started, waiting, complete) or `pointer` (a file the owner should know about, a shot, a review verdict), each cut to 600 characters. Steps, actions, decisions, commits, heartbeat and `worktree-watch:` lines are dropped, and a burst with nothing left sends no message, so it wakes nobody. A subscription you make yourself with the `follow` tool still gets every line. Test: `node Servex/Follow-kind.test.mjs`; cost: `node Server/FollowCost.mjs` (the rule and the measured numbers: `public/framework/ai/doc/task-buckets.md`).
 
+## A follower's ack does not wake its parent
+
+A followed line reaches the follower through `agents.send` (the same message queue as `send_to_agent`, `from: "servex-follow"`) and starts a turn. Nothing tells the follower to reply: when any child's turn ends, `Agents.wake_parent` sends its last words to its parent as `done: …` with a `[from: <child> · reply to: log agent-<parent>]` header, so every "nothing for me" woke the parent. Every message put on the agent's queue (`AgentQueue.push`, so the first prompt, `/compact` and held replays too) is recorded in `kinds`: true when `Agent.send` marked it as a followed line. Each result shifts one entry and judges by it: a turn started by a followed line that ends with under 200 characters of text and not `BLOCKED` skips the wake. A longer answer, `BLOCKED`, an error or a stop still wakes the parent. The wake still writes the parent's inbox and the landed task's "Next:" note; only the message to the parent is skipped (test `node Servex/agents/Follow-ack.test.mjs`). A follower with news should `send_to_agent`; a short reply to a followed line is read as an ack. Known limit: the list assumes the SDK ends each queued message with its own result; if it ever merges two into one turn, or a `priority: "now"` message does not end the running turn with its own result, the list slips by one; an awaken starts a fresh list.
+
 ## An agent following its own log: `skip_by` and `heard`
 
 `follow({agent, path, skip_by: ["<agent id>", …]})` drops every line whose top-level `by`, or `chat.from.agent`, is in `skip_by`, so an agent tailing its own session file is not woken by its own replies (`Follow.without`; test `node Servex/Follow-skip.test.mjs`). `heard: true` is the allow-list for a session seat (`Follow.heard`): only the owner's chat lines, `{place}` lines and Question items are delivered, since the server also writes `sent`, `refined`, `quiet` and `skip` lines into the same file. Both are set when the subscription is made and not updated on an existing one. The smart voice seat uses it in tail mode: [wake-policy.md](/framework/ux/Dictate/doc/wake-policy.md). A real run showed a session reads its new lines this way verbatim, about 3 s after they are written (the `updates` tool is for external sessions only; a spawned agent gets the lines as messages from `servex-follow`).
